    "n_faq_content_q8XJzU": {
      "type": "n_faq-content",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_hCeHLk": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "What are the benefits of Micro-Infusion?",
            "text": "<p>The stamping action of the Micro-Infusion device creates tiny micro-channels on the surface of the skin, helping to enhance the absorption of active ingredients and visibly refresh the complexion.<br/><br/>The serum you choose during your Micro-Infusion treatment will deliver visible results over time. The device uses single-use, gold-plated needles<br/><br/>You can switch up your treatments by alternating the serums every two weeks.<br/><br/>Visible benefits of Micro-Infusion may include:<br/></p><ul><li>More even-looking skin tone and texture</li><li>Glowing, refreshed-looking complexion</li><li>Softer-looking fine lines</li><li>Skin that feels renewed and rejuvenated</li></ul>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_qRAjhJ": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "When will I see results?",
            "text": "<p>Micro-Infusion treatment is an effective skin-boosting step, and many users report a visible radiance boost, glowy-looking complexion, and skin that feels more hydrated within a day or two after their first treatment. Individual results vary.<br/><br/>The more consistently you use the treatment, the more visible improvements you’ll likely notice over time. This easy-at-home facial is perfect to use a day or two before a big event, when you want your complexion to look and feel refreshed.<br/><br/>Don’t forget to keep up with your everyday skincare routine to help maintain the results of your Micro-Infusion treatment and keep your skin looking its best long-term<br/><br/><strong>Timeline of Visible Results<br/></strong><br/><strong>After 1–2 Treatments (Weeks 1–4):</strong></p><ul><li>Typically users experience mild redness post-treatment that settles within a few hours – this is a normal response!</li><li>Skin looks more hydrated, plumped, and refreshed.</li><li>Complexion appears smoother and more radiant.</li></ul><p><strong>After 4 Treatments (Around 8 Weeks):</strong></p><ul><li>Fine lines begin to appear softened.</li><li>Skin tone looks more even and bright.</li><li>Hydration feels longer-lasting.</li></ul><p><strong>After 6+ Treatments (12 Weeks and Beyond):</strong></p><ul><li>Complexion looks clearer and more balanced.</li><li>Skin looks firmer.</li><li>Texture appears smoother and more refined.</li><li>Overall skin looks more youthful.</li></ul>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_663VzC": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "How often can I do this treatment?",
            "text": "<p>We recommend a Micro-Infusion treatment every 2 weeks for the best results!</p>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_awj7Em": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "How do you open the serum ampoule?",
            "text": "<p>Our serums come sealed with aluminum to ensure the serum stays sterile for treatment.</p><p>[image]</p><p></p><ol><li>Firmly hold the ampoule bottle. Find the arrow on the cap lid and flip to open from the end where the arrow is located.</li><li>Once the seal has been broken, hold the cap and steadily bend the silver seal away from the serum ampoule until it almost snaps off.</li><li>Peel back the silver seal from around the top of the serum ampoule and dispose of it.</li><li>Remove the rubber stopper and pour the serum into your Micro-Infusion device.</li></ol><p>If you're mixing serums for your treatment, put back the rubber stopper on the vial to save the remaining serum for your next session!</p>",
            "section_id": "",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/faq-1.webp"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Txn6b6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "How many treatments do I get out of one Micro-Infusion vial?",
            "text": "<p>Each treatment uses one single-use needle head and one full serum ampoule. Dispose of the needle head after every treatment.</p>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_YBQCFb": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "Can I use any serum with my Micro-Infusion device?",
            "text": "<p>No. We recommend using only Qure serums specifically formulated for the Micro-Infusion System.</p><p>The serum formulation, consistency and viscosity are selected and tested to work with the Micro-Infusion needle head and serum-delivery system for appropriate flow and treatment performance. Other serums may have a different viscosity, ingredient profile or formulation that has not been tested for use with the device and may affect flow, performance or skin compatibility.</p><p>Not all serums are suitable for Micro-Infusion. We have developed our serum ampoules for use with Qure's Micro-Infusion System. They are formulated without fragrance.</p>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_G8KdpL": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "How do I clean the device?",
            "text": "<p>Once you've finished stamping your way to brighter and plumper skin, follow the below cleaning instructions:</p><ul><li>Twist off the needle head with the cap attached and safely dispose.</li><li>Wash the chamber out with water and gentle cleanser.</li><li>Let the device air dry completely, on a clean surface, before packing away.</li><li>Open a brand new needle head packet and attach the needle head onto the device. Ensure hands are clean and don't open the cap of the needle head.</li></ul>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_XgmPhV": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "Which serum should I choose, and can I use both in one treatment?",
            "text": "<p>Choose the serum that best matches your main skin concern:</p><p><strong>Rejuvenating Serum:</strong> Designed to hydrate, plump the look of skin and soften the appearance of fine lines and wrinkles.</p><p><strong>Brightening Serum:</strong> Designed to improve the appearance of uneven tone, dark spots and discoloration for a brighter, more even-looking complexion.</p><p>Use one serum per Micro-Infusion treatment. If you want to target both concerns, alternate between the Rejuvenating Serum and Brightening Serum with each treatment, performed every two weeks.</p>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WRYG99": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "What should I do before and after a treatment?",
            "text": "<p>Before treatment:</p><p>1. Start with thoroughly cleansed skin and clean hands.</p><p>2. Patch test before your first full treatment.</p><p>3. Avoid retinol, exfoliating acids (AHAs, BHAs, PHAs), Vitamin C and alcohol-based toners for at least 48 hours beforehand.</p><p>4. Do not perform Micro-Infusion over active acne, open wounds, broken or irritated skin.&nbsp;</p><p>After treatment: Leave the serum on overnight and keep your routine simple. Avoid makeup, harsh skincare and direct sun exposure immediately after treatment. From days 2–3, use a gentle cleanser and moisturizer, continue daily SPF 50, and avoid retinoids, exfoliating acids, Vitamin C, excessive heat, sweating, steam rooms, saunas and swimming while your skin settles.</p>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_jiNXWP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "Who should not use Micro-Infusion, and what reactions are normal?",
            "text": "<p>Mild redness, slight sensitivity and a warm or tingling feeling can occur immediately after treatment. This is a normal temporary response and should typically settle within a few hours.</p><p>Do not perform Micro-Infusion over active acne, open wounds, broken or irritated skin. Do not use Micro-Infusion if you are pregnant or breastfeeding. You should also seek professional advice before use if you have a history of post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation, particularly sensitive skin, or an underlying skin or medical condition.&nbsp;</p><p>Stop use and seek medical advice if you experience significant swelling, a rash, blistering, severe or persistent redness, or significant pain. If symptoms are severe or worsening, contact a healthcare professional.</p>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_AqchJX": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "The serum or needle head is not dispensing. What should I do?",
            "text": "<p>This is usually the serum sitting away from the needles, and it is easy to fix.&nbsp;</p><p>Try these steps in order:</p><ol><li><strong>Let the serum reach the needles.</strong> After you attach the needle head, hold the device upside down for 1 to 2 minutes so the serum flows into the needle head.</li><li><strong>Tilt the device.</strong> While you stamp, keep the serum at the needle end. Lean your head back slightly, or tilt the device up towards the ceiling, to help the serum move through the needles.</li><li><strong>Give it a tap.</strong> Put the lid back on, hold the device upside down, and firmly tap the end a few times to push the serum down towards the needles.</li><li><strong>Check your pressure.</strong> Use light pressure. Pressing harder does not help the serum flow.</li><li>&nbsp;Loosening the needlehead slightly can also help with serum flow.</li></ol><p>Please do not reuse a needle head after a treatment, even if it looks clean. Each needle head is single-use.</p><p>If the serum still will not come through, or the vial or device looks damaged, contact us through the <a href=\"https://qureskincare.customerdesk.io/#rp-customer-widget-home\" title=\"https://qureskincare.customerdesk.io/#rp-customer-widget-home\">Help Center</a> with your order number and a short video or photo showing the problem. We will help you sort it.&nbsp;</p>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_item_qAGj8i": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "secure_strap": false,
            "heading": "Can I buy extra needle heads or serum refills?",
            "text": "<p>We don’t sell needle heads on their own. Each treatment is designed to use one serum vial with one single-use needle head, so they are supplied together as a set. Using a needle head more than once is not recommended, and using it with leftover serum from a different vial is not part of the treatment.</p><p>If you’d like more treatments, you can buy a Micro-Infusion supply with the number of months that suits you. Every supply includes a needle head and a serum vial for each treatment.</p>",
            "section_id": ""
          }
        }
      },
